# Always git commit

After finishing a coherent unit of work the user requested, create a git commit for those changes in the same turn — do not wait for an explicit “commit” ask.

Follow the repo’s normal commit protocol (status/diff/log, stage relevant files, HEREDOC message, no secrets, no Co-authored-by Cursor / Made-with Cursor trailers, no amend unless the usual amend conditions apply, no push unless asked).

Skip only if there is nothing to commit, or the user explicitly said not to commit.
